# Assessment Binder section content proof (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08): comprehensive / enclave Playwright matrices reported
Assessment Binder / auditor-binder **PASS** from instance list, section-tree
clicks, export toolbar, honesty banner, and tab chrome — while section bodies
stayed empty, placeholder, or never sampled. Chrome and IAM-gated page load
are not auditor package proof.

## The rule

> **Never claim Assessment Binder, auditor-binder, auditor package, living
> binder, or comprehensive enclave binder coverage “works,” “fixed,” or
> “PASS” from list / tabs / export chrome alone. For each binder instance
> in scope (or every lab binder when claiming full coverage), sample every
> section (or a documented full section set) and assert non-empty
> auditor-usable narrative and/or findings — minimum length, not
> placeholder. A live IAM session is required (not Admin-Token-only).**

Layout visibility remains required per
[`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc);
it is **not** binder content acceptance.

## When this rule applies

Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive): comprehensive test, full product / enclave
test, Assessment Binder tested, auditor-binder PASS, auditor package works,
living-doc binder complete, C3PAO binder QA, `/enclave/auditor-binder`
coverage.

Does **not** force full section sampling for a narrowly scoped chrome /
layout fix that explicitly scopes out binder content (still must not claim
binder or auditor package works).

## Required preflight

1. **IAM session** — `seedIamSessionFromLogon` / real `/login` password
   logon with a documented lab identity (**liebsoft** / **lanicu** /
   seed superadmin — **never `phil`**). Admin-Token-only SPA init that hits
   AuthBound / 401 on binder APIs is **FAIL** for binder claims.
2. **Binder route** — open `/enclave/auditor-binder` under that session;
   instance list loads.
3. **Scope** — name every binder instance under test, or state “all lab
   binders” and enumerate them from the list API / UI.

Keep lab services alone unless restore is required. No `cargo clean`.

## Required content proof (minimum set)

Before claiming binder / auditor package / comprehensive enclave binder PASS,
complete **all** of:

| # | Exercise | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **IAM session** | Live logon seed; binder APIs succeed without token-only bypass |
| 2 | **Instance scope** | Named binder id(s) or full lab inventory |
| 3 | **Section sample** | Every section in scope (or documented full outline set) opened once |
| 4 | **Auditor-usable body** | Per section: narrative and/or findings text with length **≥ 40** characters after trim; not placeholder (below) |
| 5 | **Export honesty (optional add-on)** | If export is claimed: format control usable + honesty banner — still **does not** replace §4 |

Placeholder / empty patterns that **fail** content proof (case-insensitive
substrings or exact empty):

- Empty / whitespace-only HTML or text
- `TODO`, `TBD`, `placeholder`, `lorem ipsum`, `coming soon`, `do-not-ship`
- Raw template tokens only (e.g. `{section_title}` with no prose)
- Status chip `draft` / `gap` with **no** operator or auto-fill body of ≥ 40 chars

Honest **BLOCKED** is required when a section is intentionally out-of-scope
or the lab has no findings seed — label the section and reason; do not
promote chrome PASS over empty body.

## Forbidden “false green”

Do **not** treat any of these alone as Assessment Binder / auditor package
success:

- Instance list / New / Rename / Delete chrome
- Section tree select without body assert
- Tab switches (Section / Params / History / Export) heading-only
- Export toolbar visible / honesty banner visible without §4 content
- Nav crawl or enclave menu green that never opens section bodies
- Admin-Token-only binder open (AuthBound papered over)
- Living-doc wizard click without saved narrative/findings length check
- Citing Connect / messaging / Jump chrome matrices as binder content proof

## Canonical specs (content path — extend, do not chrome-only)

Prefer IAM-seeded embedded-live specs under `pim-offline-server/ui/e2e/`:

- `auditor-binder-living-doc-embedded-live.spec.ts`
- `auditor-binder-export-persona-embedded-live.spec.ts` (export claims)
- `auditor-binder-layout-embedded-live.spec.ts` (layout only — **not** content PASS)

New comprehensive claims MUST add or run asserts that walk sections and
check body length / non-placeholder — not only wizard button visibility.

